%% Sequence Diagram for Youth Account Management (Mermaid)
sequenceDiagram
  participant Parent as Parent/Guardian
  participant UI as Dashboard UI (React/Angular)
  participant API as Youth Account API (Node.js/Java)
  participant Auth as Auth Service (OAuth2)
  participant AccountSvc as Account Service
  participant PaymentSvc as Payment Service
  participant TransactionSvc as Transaction Service
  participant DB as Database (PostgreSQL)

  %% Dashboard access
  Parent->>UI: Login & access youth dashboard
  UI->>Auth: OAuth2 token request
  Auth-->>UI: Access token (RBAC: parent)
  UI->>API: GET /api/youth-accounts/{id}/dashboard (token)
  API->>Auth: Validate token & RBAC
  Auth-->>API: Valid (parent)
  API->>AccountSvc: Fetch account info
  AccountSvc-->>API: Account details
  API->>DB: Fetch spending limit, settings
  DB-->>API: Limit, settings
  API->>TransactionSvc: Recent transactions
  TransactionSvc-->>API: Transaction list
  API-->>UI: Dashboard data (balance, limit, txns)
  UI-->>Parent: Render dashboard

  %% Fund allocation
  Parent->>UI: Initiate fund transfer
  UI->>API: POST /api/youth-accounts/{id}/fund-transfer (token, payload)
  API->>Auth: Validate token & RBAC
  Auth-->>API: Valid
  API->>AccountSvc: Validate source, check balance
  AccountSvc-->>API: OK/insufficient funds
  API->>PaymentSvc: Initiate transfer
  PaymentSvc-->>API: Transfer result
  API->>DB: Update balance
  DB-->>API: Updated balance
  API-->>UI: Transfer result
  UI-->>Parent: Show transfer status

  %% Set spending limit
  Parent->>UI: Set/update weekly limit
  UI->>API: PUT /api/youth-accounts/{id}/spending-limit (token, payload)
  API->>Auth: Validate token & RBAC
  Auth-->>API: Valid
  API->>DB: Update limit
  DB-->>API: Confirmation
  API-->>UI: Limit updated
  UI-->>Parent: Show confirmation

  %% View transaction history
  Parent->>UI: View transactions
  UI->>API: GET /api/youth-accounts/{id}/transactions?startDate=&endDate=&page=&pageSize= (token)
  API->>Auth: Validate token & RBAC
  Auth-->>API: Valid
  API->>TransactionSvc: Fetch transactions
  TransactionSvc-->>API: Transaction list
  API-->>UI: Transaction data
  UI-->>Parent: Render transactions

  %% Error handling (example)
  API-->>UI: 403 Forbidden / 400 Bad Request / 500 Error (structured error)
  UI-->>Parent: Show error message